WEBVTT

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:29.160
The hat! The hat for Mr. Farnando!

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.080
The hat! The hat!

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:31.810
It's coming.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.110
The hat! My hat!

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:35.050
You too? Your hat, sir?

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.740
You didn't hear me. My hat, for God's sake!

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:38.680
Right away, sir.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:45.480
Sorry, but since Don Juan had also asked for the hat, right away...

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:46.160
Are you coming or not?

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:48.240
I have a job.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.660
Niñi, please, the hat! I have to go out!

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.040
And take care of the gentleman.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:59.500
I'm taking care of the comedians of the King's Company who have come to rent the clothes.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.840
Are you going to attend? I need a suit for a dance.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.180
I said that later the officer will attend, he has not heard me.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:05.040
And excuse me sir.

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:06.920
And you give me the hat, yes or no?

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.080
Take it, and you're going to leave with the work that there is.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:09.900
I have to go to a sepulcher.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:11.520
Besides, I don't have to go to the sequence.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:13.760
How long is the joke going to last?

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:14.280
What joke?

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:18.320
And I to the boss then.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.400
With what hat?

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.160
Distracted I am, I thought you had already given it to me.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:32.800
Oh, it's your fault!

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:36.000
It seems a lie that with so much hair you have such a small head!

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:36.960
Is it my fault?

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.450
So much hurry, so much hurry, they make me wrong!

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:41.610
Hey, little one!

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:44.120
Either you give me a hat with a feather,

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:45.540
or here it will stink so much!

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:46.580
And what do you want?

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:47.750
I want a dance.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:48.740
Don't ask him.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:51.690
What I want?

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:52.170
Yes?

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:53.850
A butterfly suit.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:54.830
For some kid?

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.480
No, miss, for me.

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:56.900
Oh?

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.970
No, sir, for your husband, the only thing we have is...

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:05.360
No, miss, please. I want a butterfly one, even if it's too small for me.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:05.700
Okay.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:06.440
Me?

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:08.390
Yes.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:09.530
I'm going to get one.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.680
Try a butterfly one, sir.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:12.920
With pleasure, little girl.

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:14.030
Do I give you the measurements?

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:17.870
No, what you have to give is the cell and 40 pesos for the stamp.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:18.350
Did you hear?

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:19.280
Yes, little girl.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:22.990
And you, if in the dance they break your wings, you get a discount for the stamp, eh?

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:29.970
Carmen's son, from...

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:30.480
Mancinelli.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:31.240
He's late.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:32.990
The buttons are missing.

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:36.710
Oh, you're going to hear Mancinelli with the character he has. Tell them to hurry.

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:37.570
Excuse me.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:39.390
Tell me, miss. And the pen?

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:41.110
Take it. How heavy.

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:45.640
Miss, I want a pen for my hat. And what do I do?

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:48.500
Go to the market and ask for a pen.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.390
Enough. You are an insolent.

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:54.010
Scream at me. I tie you up.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:55.010
I am an artist.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.450
Laugh. Artists are the ones who sing.

00:03:58.650 --> 00:03:59.580
What do they say?

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.960
And you, who are you to judge about art?

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:08.440
Who am I? Me to talk about...

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:09.780
Minnie is an artist of soul.

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:11.010
And a daughter of an artist.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:12.060
She sang opera.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:15.060
Do you want to stop fooling around and treat us like people?

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.380
I can't, sir. I have to finish the dress of the Mancinelli.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.160
And why don't you leave that for the tailor?

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:22.020
The tailor is sick, so you know.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.380
Don Teodoro is sick?

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.400
Yes, as you hear, yes, sir.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:26.140
Very sick?

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:28.490
With the tenor.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:29.760
It's worse.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.200
Very good, baby.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:31.860
Twelve.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:41.570
Are you sure?

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:42.090
Time.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:45.300
Well, it's twelve.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:46.750
Cigarette, because we're leaving.

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:47.550
Today is Saturday.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.210
But girls, the manchinette.

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:52.910
Sarpilla, until Monday.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:53.570
Don't worry.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:54.370
Until Monday we finish.

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:55.290
Bye.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:56.030
Girls.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:58.490
What happened?

00:04:58.490 --> 00:04:58.690
What happened?

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:01.760
Did the girls leave?

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:03.340
Yes, and the comedians?

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:03.880
Well.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:05.110
Aren't you going to have lunch?

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:07.150
I can't, Adriana, I have to finish this.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:09.030
He tried on the butterfly costume.

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:10.090
He's trying it on himself.

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:11.860
In the meantime, I'll keep him company.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:12.840
Do you like it?

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.240
Keeping him company?

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:15.560
I love it.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.560
No, I'm asking about the dress.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:18.940
It's beautiful.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.000
And I understand this.

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:22.860
For some reason, my name is Carmen.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:23.740
Carmen?

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:26.540
Yes, didn't you know? Carmen Rodríguez.

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:27.710
Isn't Nini her name?

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:28.750
Diminutive.

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:29.450
Carmen?

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:31.560
Carminina, Ninina, Nini.

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:32.760
How delicate.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.100
Do you know why they gave me that name?

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:35.560
No.

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:38.240
Because I was born in an interval of the opera car.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:39.310
In a dressing room?

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:41.400
It must be in the vestibule.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:45.160
Oh, that's why I have such a great expectation to be an artist.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:46.640
Did you inherit it from your parents?

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:47.390
Yes.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.080
Mom was a singer.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:50.490
Dad was a singer.

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:51.550
Singer too?

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:53.230
No, low in stature.

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:54.430
I also inherited it.

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:56.920
But what a hungry face you have.

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:58.800
Why aren't you going to have lunch, poor thing?

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:00.960
That's not what I have in me.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:02.460
No? And what?

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:04.080
Don't you see it?

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:04.730
No.

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:07.900
I'm in love.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.120
Don't tell me. And from whom?

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:11.940
From you.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:15.420
From me? Thank you, Adrián.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.750
I'm sorry, but I have another situation.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:20.600
At the end of the year, which one? I'm going to raise my salary.

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:22.690
That's not it, Adrián. Don't be offended.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:24.050
But you're not mine.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.220
And what's your type, more or less?

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:28.520
I don't know. A sensational man.

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:29.610
A hero.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.620
A champion, a bullfighter.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:35.120
I see a bullfighter in the cinema and I run cold for the stage.

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:40.110
You don't call yourself Carmen like I do if you don't understand me.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:44.860
The man who fights with the land and playing his life, he gives it to his mother.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:50.520
And you think that not being a bullfighter there is no case?

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:51.380
There is no case.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:53.570
But if there are no bullfighters here?

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:55.060
Some will come one day.

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:56.020
If there are no races?

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:56.680
Come on!

00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:59.470
That there are not? And now there will be bulls.

00:06:59.570 --> 00:06:59.890
Come on!

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:05.480
Lini, where have you been?

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:08.320
I know, the hat. It was a mistake.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:10.120
What hat? The suit!

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:11.790
Oh, I would have also made a mistake.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:13.310
The Mancinelli's suit.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:13.990
Ah, for Monday.

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:16.050
I'm finishing it and it will arrive perfectly.

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:17.210
It won't arrive.

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:18.280
What do you know?

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:18.960
It's the theater's alarm.

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:22.700
Even if it is, then it's ready and Carmen goes on Monday.

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:24.300
Carmen doesn't go on Monday.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:25.320
She doesn't go on Monday.

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:29.490
I have more time to finish it than she doesn't go on Monday.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:37.680
this night. He's sick of the terror of Traviata. This night Carmen is going and the dress is not going to be.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:44.000
The dress is going to be. No, because the cutter is sick. It doesn't matter because I'm going to finish it.

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:51.380
Do you think you know? It's my job, sir, because I have a job for you to see. I also have it. I don't know, what is it?

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:57.760
It's been ten years since I've told the artists what the directors solve and the directors what the artists say.

00:07:57.920 --> 00:07:59.980
Yeah, that's what I'm talking about.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.370
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:02.390
And do you call that a warning?

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:03.650
Yes, ma'am. Why?

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:06.170
Because in school we called it differently.

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:08.350
Don't waste my time, please.

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:10.340
Are you going to come and get the clothes?

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:11.100
It's not my obligation.

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:12.040
Well, then a girl will take them.

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:13.710
There are no girls, Mr. Juan.

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:15.710
It doesn't matter. If you want, I'll take them, Mr. Juan.

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.730
No, you have to go and get the tenorio.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:19.150
And if they don't pay you, make it and take it.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:20.660
Don't worry, Mr. Juan.

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:22.640
I'll take it and I'll see the agency.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:23.300
Impossible.

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:27.230
You know that the Martinelli always wants a girl to send him the dress.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:28.680
I'll try it on.

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:29.810
You're going to be crazy.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.170
Why not? Mancinelli has three abs, and I have only one.

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:35.750
He'll win with the model.

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:36.510
You think so?

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:37.590
I'm sure.

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:41.290
And without another one, I'll take this opportunity to put myself in your order.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:42.770
This one, this one, this one.

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:43.310
Good afternoon.

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:43.810
Good afternoon.

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:45.180
Do you think you'll make it?

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:47.210
If you help me, we'll finish it running.

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:48.390
What running? Flying.

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:50.920
Miss, do you think I can't fly?

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:51.500
Why?

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:53.200
Because I think I have very few wings.

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:58.190
If you don't go back to the first interval, it's because you've been hit against the wall, I remember.

00:08:58.830 --> 00:08:59.470
Fly, fly.

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:01.150
And you, look at me.

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:07.290
But keep that in mind, because if not tonight, Carmen's cigarette suit will smell like tobacco.

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:13.250
I don't care.

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:15.320
No, you can't go through here.

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:16.610
What if you can know?

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:18.350
This is the entrance for the artists.

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:21.450
Come on, just in case I see Minelli.

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:22.950
Impossible, tonight she sings.

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:23.690
Oh, what a novelty.

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:27.310
If she didn't sing tonight, neither I, nor this, nor the dress would be here.

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:28.450
Oh, you bring the dress?

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:29.730
Yes, I'm going to bring it.

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:32.410
The police can't find her.

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:34.450
Why, instead of saying stupid things, she doesn't run away?

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:35.150
They're waiting for her.

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:37.200
I respect the ladies.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:40.200
Lucia Levita is the Count of Monte Cristo.

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:41.580
Let's go, Adrián.

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:46.720
Give me the box.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:47.860
No, you accompany her to the dressing room.

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:49.240
That's what they say. And where could it be?

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:52.170
At least we know that here are the women's dressing rooms.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:52.690
I'll knock.

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:53.330
Right away.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:03.400
I have a knot in my tie, that's why the lady's voice is coming out.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:04.400
It's almost 20.

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:05.220
Wait.

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:07.160
Let's ask this fireman.

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:08.700
Sir, Mr. Fireman.

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:10.830
Miss, they are dragons.

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:12.960
They are Carmen Rodríguez.

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:16.280
And, please, the chameleon of Mrs. Mancinelli.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:16.920
That part.

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:18.220
The number 8.

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:19.240
Thank you very much.

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:23.670
Well, you can go.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:25.150
No, I would like to stay.

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:27.350
Go and ask for the tenorio.

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:27.930
But I'll be right there.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:29.420
I invite you to dinner later.

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:29.960
To a good dinner.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.020
Thank you.

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:32.700
It's not my fault not to be rich.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.300
I can't even go get it.

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:37.200
Well, as long as you go like this.

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:39.660
From the Astrerian!

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:43.900
She seems angry.

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:45.580
No, it's the impostor's voice.

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:47.080
I'll do the impostor right away.

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:51.120
Does she want to touch us?

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:52.370
No, it's a courtesy.

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:53.510
She invites me to come by.

00:10:53.910 --> 00:10:54.250
She's black.

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:05.290
Please, Mr. Dragón, give me some fire.

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:06.340
What did you say?

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:07.880
How dare you ask me for fire?

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:09.120
Don't you see I'm a fireman?

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:10.720
Yes, but like the other one.

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:11.420
What other one?

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:13.820
Don't you know it's forbidden to smoke?

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:14.770
No, sir.

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:15.570
Get out immediately.

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:16.640
Yes, sir.

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:20.480
It's true that the dress arrived at the last minute, but it's not my fault.

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:21.010
Oh, no?

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:22.050
Whose fault is it then?

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:23.120
Whose fault is it then?

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:24.640
As the function was anticipated.

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:26.440
That's why you're delaying my dress.

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:28.080
You're delaying my dress?

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:29.760
Luckily, I had this one from last year.

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:33.320
You're not going to need it, ma'am. It's expensive.

00:11:34.010 --> 00:11:35.730
And what if we run out of it in a hurry?

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:38.170
If you run out of it in a hurry, it must be a piece of crap.

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:39.730
A big piece of crap.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:42.120
And who's going to put it on for me to see?

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:42.960
Me, ma'am.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:44.670
Yes? And who else?

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:45.710
Who else?

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:48.130
If I look like a dwarf, let her try it on.

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:49.830
I'm a chorister, not a taster.

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:50.690
That's right, Tina.

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:51.830
I'll try it on.

